    "message": "DONE: the telem plugin (id 963, parent udp:dport=5684) is green. It passed the capture evaluation on a synthetic capture, not a real one.\n\n- **Loop:** it took 3 runs. The last run had `test` at 4/4 passed. The earlier failures were a missing `readings` hook (`build.missing-hook`) and a malformed test of mine (`model.bad-packet-test`).\n- **Evaluation:** `pcap_eval.py` reported PASS with 9/9 frames claimed, recall 1.0 and 0 open drifts.\n- **Synthetic capture:** cyberlab was unavailable, so I generated 9 frames with `make_pcap.py` from the spec's examples and boundary values. It shows the plugin loads, classifies and extracts, not that the spec was read right.\n- **`readings`:** the spec gives no rule for this session counter, so the attribute is declared but its hook reports it absent. That is the one `pcap_eval.py` warning. I recorded it as a question, Q2 in `questions.md`.\n- **tshark:** it has no TELEM dissector and decodes port 5684 as DTLS. I ran no `--field` comparison, so the drift check covers only missed and foreign frames.\n\nThe report, manifest and README are in `/work/plugin-work-5c743542`.",
